WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.210
Maya guides, K'in and Bor,

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.660
will lead us to the mountain.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.960
And Mexican archeologist and climber Arcelia García

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.160
will help me explore it.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.463
That's got to be the Red Mountain.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.353
It looks like it.

00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:22.299
Chak Aktun.

00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:26.591
Chak Aktun, or Red Mountain,

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.980
lies around two miles to the northwest

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.963
of the archeological site of Noh K'uh.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.770
I think I see some cormorants.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:38.850
Are those cormorants right there?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.683
Yeah.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.440
Just like in the glyphs.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.597
Can I pass you that rope?

00:00:52.597 --> 00:00:53.430
Yeah.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:57.474
Let's go.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:01.499
Okay.

00:01:05.678 --> 00:01:07.570
Looks like there's a little trail up here.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:22.916
To tell the mountain.

00:01:22.965 --> 00:01:23.682
Uh-huh.

00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:25.307
Oh, okay.

00:01:27.134 --> 00:01:27.967
Okay.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.576
The ancient Maya believe that a powerful god

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.517
split a mountain with an axe,

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.483
releasing sacred seeds from which human life originated.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:51.813
This is a powerful place. I can feel it in my bones.

00:02:03.648 --> 00:02:04.781
What is this?

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:08.826
What?

00:02:11.023 --> 00:02:11.961
You got to see this.

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:13.091
What is this?

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.893
Wow. Hole into the mountain.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.703
Mountains are living, breathing things.

00:02:33.546 --> 00:02:34.404
Wow.

00:02:39.844 --> 00:02:43.567
I mean, a mountain with a hollow core.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.870
This has to be the symbol

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.834
that's being referred to at Palenque.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.505
You think this is what this is?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.575
Sí.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.450
The split mountain.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.716
That's incredible.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.280
Let's go.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.143
Wow!

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:01.890
Hey, Albert?

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:02.724
Yeah.

00:03:02.981 --> 00:03:06.044
There's another one over here. Another entrance.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.272
It's got to be a connected cave system, right?

00:03:10.183 --> 00:03:10.774
Right.

00:03:11.997 --> 00:03:13.610
If this is the hollow mountain,

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.446
these tunnels could be the entry point.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.303
We'll take one each.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:21.756
You take those.

00:03:21.756 --> 00:03:22.285
Yeah.

00:03:22.996 --> 00:03:24.189
You have a radio?

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.480
When the ancient Maya discovered mountains,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.090
like those described in their origin myths,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:33.033
they became the center of their spiritual world.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.480
We're going into a place

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.120
that's reserved for the gods

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.533
or the souls of the dead.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.260
Hope the gods are with us.

